(That header is about THIS FILE, which is a licence pointer — repository
metadata, like the other per-directory LICENSE files, so it carries the same
MIT OR Apache-2.0 as they do and ../REUSE.toml lists it with them. What it says
about the directory's contents is below.)

Everything in tests/ — the committed half of the harness: per-tick hash chains,
canonical playbooks, verifier reports, path hashes, geometry digests, feed logs
and vista PNGs under `tests/golden/<area>/` — is licensed under

  GNU General Public License, version 3 or later
  (../LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt)

These files are produced by the game's own code and read only by it, so they
take the game's licence, the same as crates/ and xtask/. Most of them cannot
carry a header at all — a .txt hash chain, a .png — which is what ../REUSE.toml
is for.

FOUR CARVE-OUTS are `MIT OR Apache-2.0`, for the same reason crates/proto is
one: a third party writing a playbook tool needs them as the reference they
are. `tests/golden/proto/**` is canonical gp.v1 JSON and views of the schema —
the same public surface as proto/**; `tests/golden/plan-core/**` is the
canonical form of the example playbooks; `tests/golden/schema/**` is the
generated JSON Schema that get_schema serves; and `tests/golden/operator/**` is
the playbooks the built-in operator seals from library/'s permissive templates.
../REUSE.toml carries each carve-out as an annotation below the tests/** one,
so it wins for those paths.

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this directory shall be licensed as above, with no additional
terms or conditions, and signed off under the Developer Certificate of Origin
1.1 (../docs/DCO.txt).

The repository-wide scheme is described in ../LICENSE and ../docs/LICENSING.md;
the machine-readable manifest is ../REUSE.toml.
